    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.30.1</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:56:03 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>23001</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.30.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Clicking a duck, in the pond's inspector or in the Room, opens its tab again (it said "Couldn't open").</li><li>The Dashboard ↔ Room slide is smooth and the same in both directions: the pages move as one picture while you swipe or toggle.</li><li>+ in the pond's inspector opens a terminal there, in the pond's folder.</li><li>Reopening a long chat and the full-screen controls cost less, so the app stutters less.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.30.0</h4><p><strong>Ponds are a group chat with your ducks.</strong> Threads are now ducks: agent teammates with a name, a role and their own colour.</p><ul><li>Opening a pond shows its Dashboard; swipe with two fingers (or use the switch) to the Room, the pond's group chat. A duck's reply reads in its own words with a "files · time" chip, a question comes with A/B/C buttons, and a working duck shows what it is on.</li><li>Say what you need in the Room and a fitting duck offers to take it ("I can take this… Go"), showing where the work will run (an existing stream or a new one, which you can change). Nothing starts until you tap Go or Allow.</li><li>Ducks belong to the pond and move between streams per job, keeping a notebook of what they did. Close a duck's tab to put it off duty; find and bring back any duck from the Ducks list.</li><li>The inspector is always tabbed: Pond first (Needs you, Ducks, People, Invite), and + opens a terminal right there. Pond settings live in Settings › Ponds.</li><li>Attach pictures and files, paste images or dictate in the Room; attachments go with a job to its duck.</li><li>A reply is read the way WhatsApp reads it, and ponds show bold only when something is unread. Ducklings open as tabs; each pond takes its logo's colour as a faint wash.</li><li>The working glyph only ever appears animated, on something actually working. Idle rows show no icon.</li><li>A plain closing question is a normal finish; only lettered options make a duck need you. Approval cards lead with the decision.</li><li>Lighter on the CPU: the glyph is about four times cheaper and an idle chat is no longer re-read every two seconds. Auto-compact starts at 90% of the model's window.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.29.2</h4><ul><li>Coming back to Squeak from another Space no longer flips a finished chat to Idle and back.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
